        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Black Jack vs Latex-ite Driveway Sealer: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Pick Black Jack if your blacktop is gray, rough and open-textured, you want the heaviest rubberized, urethane-enhanced pail on the shelf, or your store only stocks the Drive-Maxx line. Pick Latex-ite if you want more square feet per pail on the label, a cure rating down to 40°F for a late-season job, or a 10-year warranty from the Ultra Shield tier. On a smooth, sound driveway that was sealed two or three years ago, the two flagship pails are close enough that prep and weather will decide the result, not the logo.
          </p>

