        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Latex-ite Ultra Shield is the better buy for most driveways: its label lists more square feet per pail on smooth asphalt, it is rated to cure down to 40°F, and it carries a 10-year warranty. Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000 is the better buy for a gray, rough driveway that needs a heavy rubberized coat, and Black Jack's five numbered tiers make it easy to match price to expectations.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever logo you choose, buy by tier and by texture, compare cost per square foot, match every pail's batch, fill cracks with the same brand's product, and spread two thin coats in warm, dry weather. Plan to reseal every two to three years, whatever the pail promises.
